# Surgical edits to upstream files, applied in this order to the pristine tree.
#
# Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored. Patches apply with zero fuzz
# (`git apply --whitespace=error`, never -3), so any upstream context change
# fails the build loudly rather than landing a half-correct hunk.
#
# GROWTH RULE: a patch that grows past a few hunks has stopped being a
# surgical edit. Promote it to a `replace` entry in overlay.map instead --
# a whole-file override is reviewable and cannot rot silently, whereas a
# large patch will conflict on every upstream touch. See docs/overlay.md.

